WEBVTT

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.110
Mark Sein and Mark Nicht, twin dock, engage!

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.280
Kazuki-senpai and Soushi-senpai?

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.330
Don't, Kazuki...

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.870
You can't use your power yet.

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:31.190
It retreated. Where?

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.090
Bird's showing no sign

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.060
of the enemy.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.780
Walker has disappeared from search range.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:15.670
No response from Solomon.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.270
Welle Shield 1 and reflective camouflage restored.

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:22.770
That's a shadow. The real
enemy is somewhere else,

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:25.890
pursuing the island and learning our powers.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:30.100
There's some other being that's
instantly relocating all that mass.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:31.990
If that's the real enemy,

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:36.300
once we locate its position, we can
find a way to counterattack.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:39.010
For now, send out Kazuki and Soushi.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.950
Then learn to understand the
power you've obtained.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.760
Prove to me that you can use this power correctly.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.330
Where are you going?

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:51.480
To see Chizuru.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:55.820
I need to know about the length of my life.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.630
Are you okay, Mai-san?

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:01.830
Yes, I was nervous, but I made it through...

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.380
This was your first time on an
operation during a battle, right?

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.160
Don't overdo it. Rest for today.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:07.010
But...

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:09.160
Resting is part of an operator's job, too.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.660
All right, just for a bit. I'll take you up on that.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:17.300
Are you two okay?

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.760
Don't just barge in...

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.200
Oh, sorry.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.140
Tomorrow, at the same time,
come for exams, just to be safe.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.060
But I'm fine!

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:27.810
Let me see.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.090
I-I'm okay, really.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:37.310
Kondou-sensei...

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:38.480
Sakura?

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.070
Just because you're a doctor, it doesn't
mean you can skip your own exams!

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:43.370
Come on, now.

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:49.380
Huh?

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:54.890
I guess even you get nervous, huh?

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.380
Until just now, I was fine...

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:01.850
Weird, huh?

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:04.070
Are you doing okay, Reo?

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.220
Of course not. I lost in a sword battle.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.550
It was a compatibility issue.

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:09.360
A loss is a loss.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:12.480
Next time... I will win!

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:16.790
Are you guys okay?

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:17.680
Rina-san!

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:18.980
We're fine.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:22.240
You have exams again tomorrow.
Don't skip them.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:24.200
Hey, what's wrong, Kaburagi?

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.270
Huh? Er... I wonder...

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.380
What? Does something hurt?

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:35.300
I... I was thinking I don't want to die.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:37.450
I'm sorry.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:41.210
It's natural that people will be lost in a fight.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.290
I got scared...

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:45.690
I'm sorry.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:47.880
Ow!

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:53.910
What do you mean by "natural"?

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:57.230
Are you saying it's obvious that
we'd lose the people we have?

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.490
U-Uh...

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:02.190
Who do you think could die and it wouldn't
matter? Who decides that?

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:03.950
Don't be stupid!

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:07.850
We're going to protect each other,
so we all survive!

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:12.000
I'll have to retrain an idiot like you!

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.080
Be ready!

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.260
Okay.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.680
Cafeteria

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:19.420
Mai?
Cafeteria

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:22.720
What about your CDC work? Done already?

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.220
I left the rest to Shao-san and Vera-san.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:28.390
You'll have to rest, then. It's part of your job.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:31.530
That's what they said, but I just
can't feel at ease.

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:37.380
Even when a pilot was hurt and nearly died,

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:39.730
I couldn't do anything!

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:45.820
I can't do anything, either.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:49.830
I'm sorry... I'm just worried about Hiro-chan.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:53.080
I can't help but wonder if they're
going through that now.

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:56.270
Hiroto-kun has more battle experience than I do.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.490
If anything had happened,

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:01.000
old man Mizoguchi would've told
us via the high-speed lines.

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:02.950
Let's believe he's safe.

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:07.550
If we lose heart, those who are
fighting will lose their support.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:12.250
Yeah.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.810
Man, how long has it been since I was examined?

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:20.020
You were on the system, right? Are you okay?

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:23.210
I thought I was gonna die.
You're amazing, Soushi.

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:24.730
The controls were perfect.

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:27.140
Limit the crossing a bit more.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:29.610
You don't have to shoulder everything yourself.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.250
You're one to talk.

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:32.320
Damn straight.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.740
I only gave some technical advice.

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:38.750
I prepared all the assimilation blockers I could.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:40.790
They should last a month.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.910
The improved Activion?

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:44.960
What about for the pilots?

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:46.880
We're producing more now.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:51.190
Take assimilation accelerators and a
standard med kit, too, just in case.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:54.990
Canon said she'll believe in you.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:57.230
Sakura told me.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:06:59.460
I believe in you guys, too.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.070
All of you come back, no matter what.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:04.480
I see...

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:08.400
Then I'll get to live much longer
than Minashiro Tsubaki.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.390
There is a way to prolong life.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:13.830
In Tsubaki-chan's time, it was just a theory,

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:14.830
but now...

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.270
I know.

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:21.250
You, Seri, and many others did your
best to research it for me.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:25.370
But you mustn't try to make me live longer.

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:29.800
The island's Mir still needs to learn more.

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:32.680
About the beginning and end of life.

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:37.850
That one certainly was unexpected.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.620
According to Tatekami-san's analysis,

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:43.230
Solomon displayed a pattern
similar to human thought.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:48.660
The odds of Minashiro Saya's personality
being reconstructed are very low.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.840
Was it resonance between the Mir and the core?

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.600
Don't worry about things here. Help at the docks.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:55.910
But, Sensei...

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:59.560
Two soldiers from the island are risking
their lives for my granddaughter,

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:01.970
who's gone out to see the world.

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:05.330
I'll also do everything I can.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:09.170
The CCTS, the Cruising Carriage Thruster System,

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:12.370
is being used to transport Sein and Nicht.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:14.860
Since we can't dispatch any additional forces,

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:18.070
all we can do is send out Fafners and pilots.

00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:20.280
Even if personnel is limited,

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:23.020
do you have to send people out like mail?

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:25.160
As long as the mechs can assimilate,

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:28.660
they can get people there more quickly
and safely than a transport vessel.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:31.820
This is the best plan we could arrange.

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:34.240
How are their vitals?

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:36.670
Thanks to the long treatment period,

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:38.440
they're tending toward stability.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.810
Simulations conducted while they
were on board the system

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:46.170
showed the odds of them being caught
in a fatal assimilation are very low.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:53.030
Makabe Kazuki once piloted the only mech
to return from a battle at the North Pole.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:57.590
We'll be forcing those two
to attempt the same thing.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:03.430
Let's put our faith in the burg engineers' judgment.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:08.310
Have all the settings in place to send
them out by morning, before dawn.

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:13.830
They're seriously going to use this?

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:18.320
It's nothing but a one-way carriage system.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.910
Its cruising ability is unmatched.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:24.160
If Sein and Nicht assimilate with it,
its performance will double.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:26.770
This is what Kazuki and Soushi would choose.

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:29.840
And they'll come home, for sure...

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:31.590
It will be an unpleasant job.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:34.260
But I guess there's no need to think that.

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:38.010
We only have tonight. It's crazy,
but we have to do it.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.150
There's no one there now.

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:53.690
Soushi-senpai... Why are you here?

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:55.070
I should ask you that.

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:59.140
After a fight, I always came here. It's just a habit.

00:09:59.140 --> 00:09:59.990
Same here.

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:06.260
I believed the reborn Tsubaki-chan
would teach me a different path,

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:10.000
besides just destroying enemies.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:11.890
It's the same for her.

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:16.930
We deem it a blessing that we must
call everything we see an enemy.

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:20.040
We talk about using lives for hope's sake.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:22.350
We're no different from Tsubaki.

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:24.620
You're right...

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:26.800
The day she was born, a battle was raging,

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:29.100
and she had to protect the island.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:32.020
It makes sense that she'd be
a bit cold toward us, right?

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.520
The day she was born, huh?

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:35.460
You have a connection with her.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.940
Tomorrow's your birthday, right?

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:40.690
I'm surprised you knew that.

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:42.890
I've studied all of the pilots' data.

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.330
Is there anything you want?

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:49.540
Where did that come from?

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:51.670
I was just trying to be thoughtful.

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:55.050
You'll give people the wrong idea that way, Senpai.

00:10:56.360 --> 00:11:02.390
Hiroto said he would bring back a hope that
would make Tsubaki-chan and me happy.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:06.200
So please come home safely, all of you.

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.040
I don't need anything else.

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:09.690
All right.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:12.520
So, have you decided on a name for her?

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:14.330
U-Um...

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:17.470
There's just one idea I had...

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:20.200
No others are coming to me, I guess.

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:21.610
Let's hear it.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:39.030
To take from one another is a blessing...

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:46.350
Welcome back.

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:49.080
There's still time before you depart.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:50.140
You should rest.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:53.560
Dad, I don't intend to die.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.010
I'll bring everyone back.

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:00.610
Along with the hope Toumi went looking for.

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:08.800
When you come back, I'll teach you
a better way to handle clay.

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:27.200
Talk to your mother before you leave.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:27.800
Sure.

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:32.420
I want this home to be a place you can return to.

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:35.270
That's my wish, and your mother's.

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:37.940
Thanks, Dad.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.410
I'm alive.

00:12:57.530 --> 00:12:59.000
My bed...

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:28.450
Pottery Shop
Makabe

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:31.490
I'm going now.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:47.970
Do you have something to tell me?

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:52.240
Accept your fate, whatever it may be.

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:54.640
To become a bridge between the people and them.

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:57.440
I've experienced the Festum world,

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:59.190
but I don't fully understand it.

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:04.690
This body was too unique to be useful in the
development of assimilation treatment.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:13.860
It's likely I'll never see the future your
heart and power bring forth.

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:16.450
But by doing this, I can feel it.

00:14:17.270 --> 00:14:20.290
It's a future you can believe in, Soushi.

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:27.300
What I believe in is the will of the island's core.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:30.720
Would it be weird if I called you my brother?

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.860
In human terms, you'd be my niece.

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:40.810
I wanted to see you off after receiving my name.

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:42.330
She told me.

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:46.360
Ask Tatekami. I know you'll like it.

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:47.620
Okay.

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:49.700
I'll be back.

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:59.900
In Tsubaki's time, all I could do
was leave everything to her.

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:02.310
This time, let's see the future together.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:05.460
Go, Soushi.

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:09.920
Report from Bird and the patrol craft.

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:11.840
No sign of the enemy within shield range.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.700
Seri, what are you doing?

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:18.670
Um, I thought you might come here...

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:20.630
I see. So?

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.770
What will you name me?

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:25.190
Well...

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:30.110
Minashiro Orihime-chan...

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:33.530
Oh, like the Star Festival.

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:36.200
Y-Yeah, yeah! Since you were born on that day.

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:40.120
I already knew it, but you
really are simple-minded.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.900
Um, what do you think?

00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:45.990
If that's your choice, it's fine.

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:46.710
Then...

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:50.050
"Minashiro Orihime" it is.

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:52.130
You may call me that.

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:55.930
The pilots are boarding.

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:58.930
Stay in blank mode until right before you get there.

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:01.320
Avoid consuming energy as much as possible.

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:02.200
Got it.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:04.690
Thanks, Canon.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:07.620
Thank me after you come home safely.

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:10.940
Bring Maya back, and all the others.

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:12.850
I will.

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:25.960
Commencing installation in cockpit.

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:36.430
Logarithmic spiral formation weak.

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:37.790
Blank mode.

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:40.100
Code formation rate just under 13%.

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:42.150
Crossing complete by both mechs.

00:16:42.150 --> 00:16:44.480
Deck flight safety system ready.

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:49.050
Assimilation confirmed between
mechs and carriage thruster.

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:54.230
They're assimilating this quickly,
even with the connection 70% blocked?

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.540
We'll be in the Fafners for a long time.

00:16:57.540 --> 00:16:59.850
Concentrate on lowering the code-formation rate.

00:16:59.850 --> 00:17:01.810
Yeah. For now, I'll go to sleep.

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:02.880
What?

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:05.830
It's easier that way, right? We have auto-pilot.

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:07.510
Nice guts.

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:10.850
We might be plunged right in the
midst of an enemy formation.

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:12.820
That'd be just as true if I were awake.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:16.300
I'll wake you when we get there.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:17.890
Until then, have a dream or whatever.

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:19.030
A dream?

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:21.720
I want to dream about when we had peace.

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:26.130
I don't know if peace ever really
existed in this world...

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:29.190
But I want to dream of the time I believed it did.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:30.470
It isn't a dream.

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:33.240
That's why we sent out Hino Miwa,

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:34.900
and why we're leaving the island.

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:38.420
For the hope that true peace will come.

00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:41.580
No problems with the passengers.

00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:44.080
Commencing transfer to Neidhöhle 10.

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:46.920
You're really using that to send them out?

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:48.720
That's insane.

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:49.940
It's our only choice.

00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:51.750
Those two can do it.

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:26.960
Wind speed, tide, course correction, all entered.

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:28.960
Carriage thruster standing by.

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:31.250
Open the Neidhöhle Gate!

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:39.810
All systems operating normally.

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:41.980
Commencing automatic countdown sequence.

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:46.770
Startup power redirected from outside to inside.

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:49.380
It's generating more energy than
planned for this operation.

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:51.560
I don't care. Continue sequence.

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:53.320
Forty seconds.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:54.900
Ignition circuits ready.

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:58.190
Shields and reflective camouflage
temporarily removed.

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:00.740
Twenty seconds. Starting up thrusters.

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:08.080
Ten, nine, eight, seven, six,

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:13.420
five, four, three, two, one.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:14.000
Zero.

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:25.560
Cruising systems operating normally.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:28.350
They're going to break the surface.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:33.910
Go!

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:45.100
Both mechs have left the search
range on the projected orbits.

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:48.340
Cutting all signals to prevent enemy pursuit.

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:52.130
Let's pray for the return of both pilots
and the expeditionary force.

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:02.550
Akira-kun, you should sleep a bit.

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:05.390
I can't sleep with all this going on.

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:09.470
The transmission from the Human Army
said we could take off in an hour

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:11.200
and that we can't use the runway.

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:12.270
It's all messed up.

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:15.140
Hey, food's ready!

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:16.730
I don't know how you can eat...

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:19.010
You can't fight a war on an empty stomach.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:21.650
A war? Whose war?

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:24.740
As long as you can't leave here, it's our war.

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:26.280
We can't leave?

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:30.030
It's been half a day since the general
said he'd secure an air route.

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:32.720
Next thing we know, a third
of the area is a battlefield.

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:35.140
I can't believe an enemy just showed up.

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:36.460
What do you mean?

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:40.120
The enemy showed up right after
Miwa-chan met the Mir, right?

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:41.460
As if someone called it here.

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:43.260
You think so, too?

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:49.700
I think there's someone able to tell
others, and the enemy, about us.

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:52.390
There's a traitor near the general?

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:55.440
Is that who's to blame for all those people dying?

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.060
It's just a guess.

00:20:57.060 --> 00:21:00.440
If we can get out of here, it'll have
nothing to do with us.

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:04.360
What is this?

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:07.780
The Mir!

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:21.590
Both of you, get in your Fafners!

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:23.880
Toumi-senpai?

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:25.950
Mizoguchi-san, prepare them for takeoff.

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:27.550
If they fly now, they'll be shot down!

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:29.240
We'll protect them.

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:30.850
If they stay here, they'll just be targets!

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:33.810
Then after that Mir comes us?

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:50.870
They're already here.

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:02.550
Our hopes are pinned on you already.

00:22:03.980 --> 00:22:05.920
You must live, Miwa.

00:22:18.550 --> 00:22:20.700
Were we only dreaming?

00:22:21.800 --> 00:22:24.470
Our wishes for peace were the
beginning of everything...

00:22:25.470 --> 00:22:29.860
That led to fighting. And war's
destruction spread ceaselessly,

00:22:30.900 --> 00:22:33.250
until it shrouded the entire world.

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:09.330
<i>Fafner in the Azure: Exodus</i>, episode 9:

00:24:09.940 --> 00:24:11.200
The Two Heroes.
